    "wmtask_epoch_compare_perconditionnorm": {
      "description": "Same as wmtask_epoch_compare but with per-condition data normalization:\neach source (epoch=1, epoch=final) is centered + noise-scaled\nindependently. Grand-mean centering (single scalar per source across\nall dims/trials/timesteps), not per-dim.\n",
      "hypothesis": "Per-condition normalization removes any cross-condition scale\nconfound (e.g. if epoch=1 activations are systematically larger or\nsmaller than final-epoch activations). The model then has to learn\nthe dynamical difference between conditions on its own, with\nmatched observable scales. If results match the cross-condition\nnormalization sweep, scale wasn't a confound; if not, it was.\n",
      "success_criteria": [
        "All cells train without divergence (no NaN train loss)",
        "Per-source mu/sigma logged in config and visible in wandb",
        "val/trajectory_loss within ~2x of cross-condition sweep at the matching cell (no big regression from per-condition scaling)"
      ]
    }
  },
